  "rel_notes": [
   {
    "t": "4.5.3",
    "d": "2026-10-07",
    "n": "* JSON path keys on Postgres are rendered inline (`data->>'key'`, `'{\"a\",\"b\"}'::text[]`) instead of as bound parameters, so `GROUP BY` and `ORDER BY` on a JSON lookup work under psycopg3, which binds each as a distinct parameter."
   },
   {
    "t": "4.5.2",
    "d": "2026-09-27",
    "n": "* `exists()` wraps the query in `EXISTS(...)` rather than replacing its columns, fixing queries that order by or filter on a selected alias, and queries on MySQL that select two columns w/the same name."
   },
   {
    "t": "4.5.1",
    "d": "2026-09-08",
    "n": "Couple little things for `EnumField`.\r\n\r\n* `EnumField` and `IntEnumField` validate member value types (`str` and `int` respectively) at field construction.\r\n* `EnumField` and `IntEnumField` default `choices` to `(value, name)` pairs derived from the enum.\r\n* Fix #3075, migration generation for `EnumField`. Generated migrations will emit the storage field type (e.g. `IntegerField`) rather than `EnumField()`.\r\n\r\n[View commits](https://github.com/coleifer/peewee/compare/4.5.0...4.5.1)\r\n\r\n<img width=\"202\" heigh"
   }
  ]
 },
